sequenceDiagram
  %% route.create on the Gateway engine: the steps of route/create.mmd (workflow operation-route-create) as host catalogue primitives composed in the Gateway (RouteEngineFlow, RouteHostSteps). ADR 0271, Routes rewrite PR B (ORB-6352).
  %% Pending A4: Caddy's recursive access needs posix.acl.ensure with `scope: tree`; a Route with access rows runs on Swamp until it lands.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: route:create
  %% kind: route.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=executor tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Route Node<br/>executor
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>executor
  CLI->>GW: route:create<br/>INSTANCE DOMAIN
  Note over GW: Validate, hold Nodes<br/>render whole files
  %%> Same guards and admitted plan as route/create.mmd (`route_create`, NativeRouteCreatePlan)
  %%> The publication hold covers every Node of the plan: site and leaf Nodes and each VPN Node with DNS work, from the reads to the guarded writes, also after an admission wait (RoutePublicationHolds)
  %%> Each account the Node's steps write for is read on the Node first (`account.read`): home, primary group and gid by NSS; pools are rendered with the group's name
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `route.create` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`, and every Node a step touches reports each step's primitive in `$KV.NODES` (the `host` family with `account.read`, agent 0.37.0), with `tls.csr_input` on the leaf Node; every build with the host family has file.ensure `source_path`, so the key copy needs no feature
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; an Ingress edge, a LAN rule, a production `.env`, awake markers, Caddy access rows, or a pool outside the two pool kinds throws `EngineUnsupported`
    %%> - the kind's own admission (RouteEngineFlow::admit) also refuses a Route with Caddy access rows, and a Node with work that lacks one host primitive, or a leaf Node that lacks `tls.csr_input`
    %%> - an owner name outside the host primitives' pattern `^[a-z_][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}$` (the Route's account or another link owner, such as `Orbit` or `Dev.Team`) keeps the whole Operation on Swamp; a name NSS answers outside it refuses at the accounts check, before any request
    %%> - production never moves: a site or leaf Node that is not an app-dev Node (app-prod, unclassified, no role), a DNS Node without the vpn role, a target Instance outside development, or an intent with a production placement or `production_control` keeps the whole Operation on Swamp
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    EN->>N: Read each account<br/>account.read · account-k
    %%> First, on each site Node: the Node's account (leaf copies, pools) and each other link owner; the recorded answer keeps a retry byte for byte, and its canonical `user` owns the account's files
    EN->>N: Read the trust anchor<br/>file.read · read-trust
    Note over EN: Check the trust anchor<br/>Gateway step · trustcheck
    %%> The anchor must hold this root or be absent; another root (a rotation) refuses here, before any request, as the Node's site step (`route.publish_failed`). During an Orbit root CA rotation, route.create is turned off in ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS until every development Node has the new root (Swamp rotates it); then it goes back on.
    Note over EN: Check the accounts<br/>Gateway step · accounts
    %%> An account NSS does not resolve now (`absent`) refuses here, before any request, so nothing has changed; the step is the Node's site step, so the Route records `route.publish_failed`
    EN->>N: Make a CSR on the Node<br/>tls.ensure_csr · csr-i
    %%> The Gateway sends the folder, its root:caddy owner, modes 0750 and 0640, and the subject; the key never leaves the Node
    Note over EN: Sign the CSR<br/>Gateway step · sign-i
    %%> As `operation:direct:certificate-sign`; a pending cancel refuses
    EN->>N: Set APP_URL and links<br/>dotenv.ensure · file.ensure
    %%> `site-node-url-k`: the last `APP_URL=` line of an existing `.env` that the account owns, replaced or appended; `site-node-link-k`: a release link owned by its account
    EN->>N: Read each pool file<br/>file.read · read-pool-k
    %%> One path, read only: absent, or present with its type, owner, mode and, for a regular file, its SHA-256; never its content. The step records the answer
    EN->>N: Write and test the pools<br/>config.apply · site-node-pools
    %%> Under `/etc/caddy/.orbit-publish.lock`: each pool rendered whole with the account's group and home, root:root 0644, with the digest its read recorded as `from_sha256` (none when absent); `php-fpm` validators from the fixed list; a failed test restores the files
    EN->>N: Start each pool<br/>systemd.unit.ensure
    EN->>N: Reload the pools<br/>config.apply · site-node-reload
    %%> The same files with the digest of the bytes the install left as their guard, so it writes nothing and refuses a change made since; validators, then each pool unit reloads on every run, as route.publish_site did
    EN->>N: Install leaf, copies<br/>file.ensure · cert-i …
    %%> `cert-i`: the signed leaf, root:caddy 0644; `current-i`: the version link; `folder-i`: the account copy's folder, root 0755 as `install -D` made it; `key-i`: the key copied on the Node (`source_path`), account 0600; `copy-i`: the leaf, account 0600; `copylink-i`: the account's version link
    EN->>N: Trust the Orbit root<br/>ca.trust.ensure · trust
    %%> The one trust anchor `orbit-managed-root-ca.crt`, root:root 0644, as main and Swamp place it; it already holds this root in every create outside a rotation, so nothing changes (the update runs only after a change); unrelated roots are never named
    EN->>N: Read the Caddyfile<br/>file.read · read-caddy
    EN->>N: Apply the Caddyfile<br/>config.apply · site-node-caddy
    %%> Under `/etc/caddy/.orbit-publish.lock`: the whole Caddyfile, root:caddy 0640, with the digest its read recorded; validated as `caddy`; Caddy reloads on every run; a failed validation or reload restores the file
    EN->>V: Read records, catalog<br/>file.read · dns-i-read-…
    %%> The reads find a link in a file's place, which the unlink step removes first
    EN->>V: Publish private DNS<br/>config.apply · dns-i
    %%> Beside the sites, after the signatures. Under `/run/lock/orbit-dnsmasq.lock`: records and catalog, root:root 0644, each guarded by its admission digest, so a payload that went stale while the create waited refuses without writing (`private_dns.publication_failed`); a file already holding the payload is kept; the `dnsmasq` validator over `/etc/dnsmasq.conf` and `/etc/dnsmasq.d`; dnsmasq and the private DNS listener restart on every run
    Note over EN: Probe the site over TLS<br/>Gateway step · probe-i
    %%> After each Node's last site step: a TLS handshake by WireGuard address, trusting only the Orbit root
    %%> A read that finds a link in a file's place runs that file's unlink step (`file.ensure` absent, never following it), and the write then sends no guard; for any other read the unlink step is done without an order (EngineSkip)
    %%> Every config.apply input comes from the admitted plan and the recorded reads, so a resend carries the same bytes, the order's identity; each step has its own `recovery_dir` under `/var/lib/orbit/executor/config-recovery` (`pool-install`, `pool-reload`, `caddy`, `dns`)
    %%> The writes overwrite whatever the Node held at the read, as main's route.create did: a pool with a numeric gid or a catalog in another key order is replaced; the guard refuses only when a file changed between its read and its write, under the Node publication hold and the lock
    alt every step succeeds
      EN->>GW: Route active<br/>same projection
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>chart name · main's code
      %%> A Node's site steps record `Install cert, publish site-<node>` with `route.publish_failed`; `dns-i` records `Publish private DNS-i` with `private_dns.publication_failed`, main's codes; a guard refusal records its chart step's code too, as main maps it
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-route-create
    %%> No step runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
    %%> A Route with Caddy access rows runs here, with Swamp's recursive access, until A4 lands; PR D keeps the old actions until then
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
